[{"id":"VRCE-6-60-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":1,"english":"Those Raksas that remained after the others had been slain, swiftly informed Răvaņa that all those foremost of Rākşasas Devantaka and the rest, Trisiras, Atikāya and others-had been slain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.426,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a5289a8336de2c5de9a246f0fac7215214c1549bcb39b1be862aba081e4835e","compact":"1a49a379426d5f324e088664609669cda607d82ca088f4bd8a6231c02809579f","nasal":"1ecbbbd787e0772cc3fac3422f03236a7cd0e71c3002cd759574894020604850"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":2,"english":"Suddenly hearing them slain, the king with his eyes charged with brine, thinking of the disastrous destruction of his sons and brothers, was extremely agonized.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.83,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c8eda15c4dcbd8cc18ae4003e4ea6370f2d7998fc579d21a34cfbf385a106598","compact":"a1bab77a2d85475102ca98a84a12bb3d5c7a8fed4b67f2c9c2c933b2c00811eb","nasal":"edd54547398a56da29a283572ada5b1edbeecbcc8ef48c7c6265b36d9014c11d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":3,"english":"Thereupon, seeing the king afflicted, and sunk in a sea of sorrow, that foremost of carwarriors-son to the Räkşasa king—Indrajit, addressed (his sire), saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.659,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a16a94cf6dd802cdbdcec09e9cd5fcb38f9e5f05d814e4321a13c8135e21b3cc","compact":"0cc403dbb16258a2fc9bbf74995e00de6dde4c8d2ee7b11de8e0b3a85435058a","nasal":"c0e9d45ecae932ae31ff2f97364c2d4a05642997550a9a7662a9525448034c7c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":4,"english":"O father, it does not behove you to be overcome with this excessive grief, inasmuch as, O lord of Nairtas, Indrajit yet breaths. Smite by the enemy of Indra, (Rāghava) can by no means save his life in encounter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.524,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab525bc07b55a49e6c749d5d968ea2078739b898c9d0f60d3b823d297581e66b","compact":"3825de093ceb1fe4b253961025d8f404e28d05516d35f14ab0f93940e902dc5a","nasal":"a24551922c08d6dbd6a5c32980a998048a683f29cdc18fafe8a587da21899930"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":5,"english":"To-day behold Rāma along with Lakşmaņa with their bodies torn with my shafts, lying down lifeless on the ground, having their persons covered with my sharpened arrows!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.663,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"973f43fb4d8ea0327373c6bb8b8e537e0b6fb1d56057bfbebcd47a7ae1518ae1","compact":"cd520930589f775e388312fa8d170be313e77caf8bfd9ad5f75233fbdad83b2a","nasal":"8b25058a5af6ea682b3c84f68cf10ab714410ecaceee352ee3edc66ad923829c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":6,"english":"Hear this vow of the foe of Indra, never swerving and instinct with prowess and divinity, this very day will I with unfailing shafts slay Rāma along with Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8195743a277af4d5426d7a60d262c9ec1092bf11bfa3cf82046d0d1bb7e726e5","compact":"88c7165c6a925a52cb130f408a54cf5136b382f1ef3631e0beda9d58810164ee","nasal":"88c7165c6a925a52cb130f408a54cf5136b382f1ef3631e0beda9d58810164ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":7,"english":"To-day let Indra and Vaivasvata and Vişnu and Rudra and Sādhyas and Vaiśvānaras (Agni) and the Sun and the Moon, behold my immeasurable prowess, terrific like that of Vişņu at the sacrificial ground of Vali.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"28ff1cd87c1b84002ca96f97f83a22ee72d4410f704bb790821733b4bd2ea54b","compact":"0949a07b184a6bb74d0937218b5973ebb8e10172aec96b5f5896f344c950089b","nasal":"37c579da8fb1b68064d707acd91c1adf4861b182581245a55cb59e55c11f0052"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":8,"english":"Having spoken thus, that foe of the lord of celestials endowed with exceeding energy, taking the king's permission, ascended a car having the velocity of the wind itself, yoked with asses, and furnished with every variety of weapons.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.604,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bc86f4f95b227d8c32902d75b5c5757a1dc0b0933aebfa563ebc037fc5d7616a","compact":"7aec532e5dd0db93ef87b5e2937342fd2e40a5d699059fa7270354144c8f4c01","nasal":"67cb977379a4fd4a1b787cfa657f