0-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":28,"english":"Having worshipped (the god of fire), that one endowed with the splendour of fire itself, that one possessed of the prowess of the great Indra and gifted with inconceivable vigour, accoutred in bows and arrows and swords and having steeds and cars and darts, disappeared in the sky.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.744,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"67314eaec4a7a373cad31d20f77b94d0007ee0858d29ee73abd99ad869b5622b","compact":"1cea96bdb7ccdcf6492f9e43cdea3fc7111439b804d3dcad369dca2a0984c2e3","nasal":"0cb2e36c63a72f4420b114dfb456b6ff8b95bb2ff06fb4561021ac27024491ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":29,"english":"Then in that encounter, leaving his army, Indrajit became suddenly invisible to the monkey-hosts—and began to shower fierce arrows, like dark clouds pouring rain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.878,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dfa62a39d44aae4964877c097812fe0310a9df7ba57b2fd2ebc625618ac2e51d","compact":"e83ab63c3151cab5539d6539e6abdc79ebd4ac36e145717fd27f4d2ad167a0b8","nasal":"be4bec48f9ae26cf034f7faaa16e39737245dcf42abc88a795a2b18d21b0095f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":30,"english":"With their persons torn by the arrows of the conqueror of Sakra, slain by his power of illusion, with their teeth uprooted, those mountain-like monkeys fell down in the field, emitting frightful cries, like a mountain smite with Indra's thunderbolt.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.804,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-48"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"69b07895c8d1f4aa723d1810946de5f41760a45c3a36595297a23f248a947e0a","compact":"cf661c3bb923933535a356ed5e584ff2c9ba1b5251b96cea4abf98c98b02e799","nasal":"12cbc1ebd74a53a4d8cd3a45bf9c03b764c801a8489f54d021f86649f389da2c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":31,"english":"In the conflict they could only see sharp pointed shafts among the monkey-ranks, but that foe of the celestial chief-the Raksasas, hidden by virtue of illusion, they could not discover there.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.607,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-49"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7339e96065655047946eeb9d04dde8c3741c4069f721f10505883953b4e9a668","compact":"1eddf2403fd92fb836e6e9340464997423d6151f312496dbb3209f7d9762f38a","nasal":"196da4b18f4db92af18acf35bf129668a2943aa4bd45ce7eedd774c1099cb1e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":32,"english":"Then the high-souled lord of Rākṣasa covered all sides with sharp-pointed shafts resembling the rays of the sun; and he rived the foremost monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-50"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cf2624a57eadd74a587ba933d59ba3af135e9b39b54155203b993afd4084dbb7","compact":"c406b5384a55015e5d20714e62a41c38758c1c2d6906498fe7bacc1807d6dfac","nasal":"e6dd3a29589f1877ec18969a280e1e33e96820388ad5552af5c63d35528b5d1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":33,"english":"And whirling darts and nistraišas and axes, flaming and having the effulgence of fire, and furnished with flames shooting forth sparks, he discharged them furiously at the forces of the sovereign of monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.674,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-51"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2687280e274a58f79d4aa4ebf178e6678c21a203ee6874f1ea50acd06e3efd6b","compact":"6dab165e35b58fa0eebca76c5bf120db49f1a1213f2fe42b457ac7188832e341","nasal":"fac31c080d986e4240d1b557ddeafb44cf2e78b2c9aae4049bfdb8569531b4ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":34,"english":"The monkey-leaders struck with Śakrajit's shafts. resembling flames, appeared like laughing Kinsukas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-52"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"40ba59f3a6194df374d8aefccdebe54fd9037f31b7d0d0ce9b42940562262f95","compact":"bbab409bdf88c1b979c11cfc55c7644f602c35d8a259bddd729bdfad46d75e30","nasal":"bbab409bdf88c1b979c11cfc55c7644f602c35d8a259bddd729bdfad46d75e30"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-60-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":60,"verse":35,"english":"They foremost of Vānaras, pierced by the missiles of the lord of Raksasas gliding towards one another and crying bitterly fell down on earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.987,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-73-53"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6060035","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"67e65e59a57f5e0498a90c88f993993f684e6d6d712d047c1a1fd41f3b7b1853","compact":"238ea1895c9e7a1f01ccf32350118b961a782bbf07fa8522ba9f51615277b369","nasal":"3ac5f803d37b4061e134076449b9e7